# Acceptance Criteria

- Every UI action mapped to its backend API.
- Every Java API has a corresponding Python API.
- Every endpoint has identical inputs and outputs.
- Business logic matches Java behavior.
- Parallel execution behavior preserved.
- Database schema validated.
- Delete-and-regenerate workflows preserved.
- Team Key usage validated throughout.
- Fix Version preserved exactly.
- Logging implemented consistently.
- Role validation implemented.
- External integrations behave identically.
- No functional regressions introduced.
- Existing Java behavior remains the source of truth.

---

# Definition of Done

The migration is complete only when:

- 100% of Java APIs are represented in Python.
- 100% of UI interactions behave identically.
- 100% of database operations match Java behavior.
- 100% of async execution paths are preserved.
- 100% of request/response contracts match.
- 100% of Team Key handling is validated.
- Fix Version remains unchanged across all layers.
- Logging is comprehensive and configurable.
- Role-based authorization is enforced.
- End-to-end regression testing passes.
- No known functional gaps remain between the Java and Python implementations.
